            <div class="step2-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Unique Contribution</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-1.png">
                <p>The Creator Archetype is one of the three archetypes who provide structure to the world.   </p>
                <p>Interestingly, and seemingly ironically, the Creator brings structure through innovation.  It seems ironic to think that innovation brings structure, but when you think about famous creator types such as Thomas Edison - who adopted a variety of technologies until he finally innovated the electric light (his creations helped everybody and provided a sense of structure to the world), then you see exactly how innovation brings about structure. </p>
                <p>Thomas Edison is a perfect example of a Creator Archetype and of how Creators focus on bringing structure to the world. </p>
                <p>Some Creators will remain lowkey with their creative endeavors choosing to create privately and sometimes will not even realize that they are actually ‘creating’ or ‘innovating.’</p>
                <p>Others might find a way to innovate and create publicly.  Regardless of your circumstances or creative style, if you are a Creator Archetype, you will find a way to express your uniqueness and individuality. </p>
                <p><strong>Creators Cannot Stand Mediocracy</strong></p>
                <p>Wherever possible, it will be important to the Creator that they are entirely original in whatever they do.  If they realize that their ideas or actions were not as creative as they first thought they’ll either raise their game, or move onto something else that will allow them to express themselves uniquely.</p>
                <p>Creators are also often perfectionists. They’ll probably have little habits and tendencies toward perfection. At home, this trait could show up in an interest in organization and the tiny decorative details in a home that have to be just so.  Creatively it can manifest in whatever masterpiece a Creator is working on.</p>
                <p>Some Creators will even use communication as an outlet for their innovation and creativity. If they do so, you can be sure that they will pay particular attention to the words they use and the ways they communicate whatever it is they want to express.</p>
                <p>However, when they have shown their creations to someone else, it will almost always be flawless. </p>
                <p>But here’s the thing, it’s rare to find a Creator who can find balance in their life. 
                <p><strong>Creation Versus Self-Maintenance</strong></p>
                <p>A Creator finds the attainment of balance difficult because if they have a project in hand, it tends to take over their entire lives. </p>
                <p>And when a project takes over, usually most of the regular routines and cycles that we all need to go through in everyday life will be forgotten.</p>
                <p>Which means that when the Creator returns to ‘reality’ after they’ve completed a project they’ll, usually have a lot of catching up to do and may have forgotten to undertake important everyday tasks during this time.</p>
                <p>It’s not so easy for a Creator to set aside their projects and prioritize everyday life, as a Creator won’t be able to settle or concentrate on anything else but the project in hand.</p>
                <p>Creators who prioritize their projects over everything else, in some ways, are similar to the Caregiver Archetype who cannot avoid feeling guilty when they can’t help somebody - it’s a challenge to switch those feelings off.</p>
                <p>And if we are going to get deep here, it’s probably worth noting that the Creator Archetype will feel frustrated or unsettled if they have not managed to create their ‘ideal life’. When we say ‘ideal life’, we mean every aspect of the Creators life so that it is perfect, unique, runs smoothly and is expressive of the Creators nature.</p>
                <p>The challenge of balancing the need to complete a project, and striving for all-round perfection at the cost of living a perfect and balanced everyday life will be unattainable for the Creator and so the Creator will feel conflicted in many ways. </p>
                <p>In this situation, with these dominant traits it will be impossible to find a successful outcome, especially since the following key traits of a Creator archetype will be permanently challenged;</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Perfectionism</li>
                    <li>Uniqueness</li>
                    <li>Self Expression</li>
                    <li>Ability To Innovate</li>
                    <li>Their Sense Of Contribution To The World</li>
                    <li>The Creator’s Self Esteem</li>
                </ul>
                <p>As you can see, the Creator experiences a huge amount of conflict. It would be advantageous to the Creator if they could resolve some of this conflict (which is entirely possible). However, if the Creator learns to practice acceptance, this is a conflict that is only resolved when the Creator and can understand why they might think and act as they do.</p>
                <p>The Creator can spend too much time on their ‘projects’ and not enough on their family, friends or on practical and important things such as taking care of their home, practicing self-care or in finding balance in life.</p>
                <p>This lack of self-awareness and balance is often why creative people typically have a reputation for living an unbalanced and ‘messy’ life.</p>
                <p>A problem that will be rife in some aspects of the Creator'ss life but not one that is overlooked - for the creator's perfectionism and need for structure will find this lack of balance entirely unsatisfactory!  </p>
                <p><strong>Always Striving for Innovation</strong></p>
                <p>So, it seems that even if the Creator does not intend to change the world consciously, their nature will always strive for innovation and individuality because they will be driven to resolve the conflict they experience in their daily life.  </p>
                <p>It’s this conflict that a Creator experiences, the push and pull between chaos, order, and creativity which brings in and settles new ideas and concepts that slowly (and in some cases significantly) change the world.  This is the Creator'ss unique contribution to the world - it's just unfortunate that they have to live the experience internally too.</p>
