            <div class="step5-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Strengths</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-2.png">                
                <p>The Creator has many strengths that they may not even appreciate themselves due to their lack of esteem and strong tendency toward attaining perfection. </p>
                <p>If the Creator can start to acknowledge both their strengths and weaknesses instead of denying them all, they’ll create the opportunity to address and manage their flaws (which are often not entirely as the Creator perceives) and embrace their strengths without punishing themselves by rejecting their strengths for not being perfect in all ways.  Here are some of the Creator’s strengths</p>
                <p><strong>Eccentric</strong></p>
                <p>Because the Creator values individuality and cannot stand to be average, you’ll often find them to be quite eccentric.  They may choose to demonstrate this eccentricity in the way that they present themselves, their home, how they operate in the workplace, or even in the types of work they choose to do and the way that they think or communicate.</p>
                <p>Last but not least you might find touches of eccentricity through the projects that they might be working on.  If you are a Creator, even if your approach is low key, you’ll definitely have some form of eccentric side that sets you apart from the rest.  This eccentricity is the way that the Creator contributes to moving their world forward.  Even if a Creator hasn’t figured out how to harness this strength yet, it’s one of the Creators strengths, for sure.</p>
                <p><strong>Has Always Got Something New To Bring To The Table</strong></p>
                <p>The Creator, because of their rejection of normality, is always thinking out of the box and they’ll always find ways to demonstrate their unique way of tackling even the most mundane features of everyday life. Such makes them socially and romantically interesting, and also admirable in the workplace.</p>
                <p><strong>Talented & Often Sought After For Their Skills</strong></p>
                <p>Creators, when they are interested in a project will quickly develop their skills so that they become expert in what they do.  They then add their unique and often innovative twist to the project they are working on to bring about a whole new outcome.  </p>
                <p>It’s the Creators unique perspective and abstract thinking that helps them stand out from the crowd,  which is why they are often in high demand in whatever industry they work within or in whatever project they are focusing on.  </p>
                <p><strong>Easily Rise To The Top Of Their Game</strong></p>
                <p>As we’ve already mentioned, Creators develop their skills so that they become the expert in whatever project they are working on; work or otherwise.  This particular talent makes Creators sought after. </p>
                <p>This strategy also helps the Creator rise to the top of their game and to others it might seem as though they did so without any problems at all. </p>
                <p>Of course, the Creator will have problems rising to the top, but they use their creativity to solve the problem.</p>
                <p>In many situations, some part of the Creators life will be extraordinary, but in some cases, Creators might not realize that they are quite as different in their thinking than others. </p>
                <p><strong>Make Wonderful Romantic Partners</strong></p>
                <p>If you can handle the Creators constant need for inspiration (which will often involve lots of travel or other forms of exploration) and you can handle their tendency toward being very biased on their own opinions, then you might find a great lover in a Creator Archetype. </p>
                <p>A Creator gives their utmost to everything that they do, which means if you are their romantic partner then you get the joy of that.  Add to the fact that Creators are emotionally aware, and sensitive to others as well as being unique in their approach.  It’s not hard to see why a Creator might have developed a reputation for being quite the catch romantically.</p>
                <p><strong>Give Their Best To Everything They Do</strong></p>
                <p>Creators cannot do anything half-heartedly, they cannot stand doing sloppy work, and are often obsessed with perfectionism, so they usually give their best.  And because the Creator is also unique in their approach and excels at driving anything that they focus on forward you can see how, when we say that the Creator gives their best in everything they do, we are not exaggerating.  In fact, that’s probably an understatement.</p>
                <p><strong>Easily Able To Form Unique And Sustainable Ideas</strong></p>
                <p>A Creator wouldn’t be a true Creator if they couldn’t form unique idea, in particular ideas that are sustainable.  </p>
                <p>Think about it, Creators are perfectionists and excel at solving problems with their unique mindset. As such, they are going to test their solutions and ideas for weaknesses and sustainability.</p>
                <p>Chances are they wouldn't even bring the idea to anybody's attention unless they’ve checked out all possible outcomes.</p>
                
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Weaknesses</h2>
                <p><strong>Creators Are Often Insufficiently Rewarded For Their Efforts</strong></p>
                <p>Even though Creators are often extremely talented, they are often not rewarded appropriately for their efforts.  You see, a Creator might be innovative, but they are not generally entrepreneurial.</p>
                <p>The entrepreneurial lifestyle is far too risky for a Creator and frankly doesn’t give them much satisfaction at all.  Creators also struggle to maintain routine and discipline which can influence how they manage their finances, or clients, etc. </p>
                <p>If a Creator can discipline themselves to master these weaknesses and focus on finding a risk free way to reap the rewards for their efforts, then it could be a completely different story.</p>
                <p>A rags to riches story probably!</p>
                <p><strong>Creators Despise Repetition</strong></p>
                <p>Clearly, the Creator has developed their innovative prowess because they like change and despise repetition. But the fact is that in life, to move forward and achieve our goals we always need some form of disciplined repetition to move forward.</p>
                <p>It sounds ironic, but repetition can be the secret to creating freedom and individuality.  Without it, we can move in circles without moving forward which in itself creates repetition!</p>
                <p>If a Creator can figure this out and find a way to introduce deliberate repetition in their life, they’ll be moving into new places that they would never reach!</p>
                <p><strong>Creators Struggle To Accept Other People’s Opinions</strong></p>
                <p>It’s not always easy for a Creator to respect or accept other people’s opinions.  This is something that can cause problems in how the Creator relates. And it can even limit the gains that they could achieve from their efforts.</p>
                <p>Life would be so much easier for a Creator if they could accept that other people have opinions and that sometimes those opinions might have some value in them too.</p>
                <p><strong>Often neglect themselves</strong></p>
                <p>Self-Care can be somewhat up and down for a Creator, depending on where they are in the process of developing their creative ventures.  </p>
                <p>If you’ve ever seen somebody who is working on decorating the house or to complete a project of some sort where nobody sees or hears from them for some time, and when they have finished, they emerge with long hair, a beard, and a drawn complexion.  Well, this is an example of a Creator.</p>
                <p>It’s so hard for a Creator to discipline things such as self-care, emotional wellness, or even basic hygiene sometimes because these things are never as important as their project.</p>
                <p>Often during a project the Creator will lose touch with reality. </p>
                <p>Combine this problem with the Creator's hatred of repetition and routine you can see how it's easy for a Creator to avoid their regular routines in favour of working on their projects.</p>
