            <div class="step6-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Greatest Challenge</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/success.png">                
                <p>The Creator Archetype's greatest challenge is to learn how to stop self-sabotaging themselves because of their need for diversity and perfection.  In doing so, they give themselves the opportunity to thrive and innovate beyond their wildest dreams.</p>
                <p>If the Creator can also learn how to bring a sense of balance into their life and can overcome their fear of being average or mediocre they will find that they enjoy life more and the challenges they face become easy to navigate while their ability to create and innovate becomes enhanced.</p>
                <p>Creators self-sabotage not just by neglecting themselves and their needs if they are working on a project but also by sabotaging their efforts in a project, even destroying them completely occasionally.  The Creators lack of self-care and productivity when they sabotage their work combined with too much focus on perfecting only one aspect of their life will play havoc with the Creators sense of perfectionism.  And could send them on downward spiral lowering their esteem and sense of self-worth in some aspects of a Creator's life this can be debilitating. </p>
                <p>Awareness is always the first step to healing or reconciliation.  If a Creator can understand and accept the parts of themselves that even they don’t like, or don’t want to acknowledge.  And if they can begin to understand why they are driven the way they are and how they can stop themselves from such self-sabotage they can build their lives around sustainable innovation instead of limiting themselves.  This way they really will step into their power and spend the rest of their lives, perfecting the art of innovation without compromising on their health, finances, or wellbeing. </p>
                <p>Which then allows them to find a way to innovate beyond the Creators wildest dreams.</p>
                <p><strong>How A Creator Archetype Can Master Their Greatest Challenge</strong></p>
                <p>As a Creator starts to understand the secrets behind their greatest challenge and build on their sense of esteem -  and as they learn the coping strategies to help them handle the fear of mediocracy and repetition.  And if the Creator can consciously balance their need for perfection in a way that doesn’t steal their confidence or pride in the things that they do the Creators life will truly be incredible.  Because all of their strengths will be unlocked and the Creator will learn how to build on them without sabotaging their work or themselves which can be a potent mix.  </p>
                <p>Many famous creators tell stories of how their famous masterpieces were sitting in the cupboard half-finished for many years before they found the inspiration to use it in a way that they were happy with.</p>
                <p>Are you a Creator who has an unfinished masterpiece in the closet?</p>
                <p>The Creator needs to accept and acknowledge themselves in order to get started with the life that they can be comfortable with. Even with the parts that they are avoiding or repressing, they can then work out strategies to help them grow in a healthy, balanced and dynamic manner.</p> 
                <p>If you are a Creator, you can learn more about how to do this in the Premium Archetype Reports.  </p>
